# CODEOWNERS -- required reviewers for supply-chain-sensitive paths
# (Phase 4, blocker 4).
#
# This ONLY takes effect where GitHub is configured to require it: repo
# Settings -> Rules (or the classic Settings -> Branches -> branch
# protection) -> "Require review from Code Owners" on a rule covering
# `main`. See PROJECT.md for the current state -- this repo currently
# allows direct pushes to `main` by design, so today this file documents
# ownership and would only start gating anything the moment that setting is
# turned on. It does not, by itself, block a direct push.
#
# .github/** is the entire publish path: every workflow, the planner, and
# the build/push script. images.yaml is the catalog deciding what gets
# built, with what base image, and under what tags. A change to either is
# exactly as sensitive as a change to the images themselves.
.github/**    @raubreywhite
images.yaml   @raubreywhite
